## The engine is not re-published here

The engine is referenced as a git submodule at `engine/`, pinned to the upstream
commit this tree is built against:

    repository  https://github.com/666ghj/MiroFish
    commit      db1bc144ff97a52e728f5ef54dfdc97c0c4ca953
    date        2026-05-24

At that commit the engine trees `backend/`, `frontend/`, `static/` and
`locales/` are byte-identical to the private source tree this repository is
exported from, apart from the files listed below.

Initialise it with:

    git submodule update --init engine


## Vendored engine files

The worker daemons import four modules from the engine at run time. Rather than
require the whole Flask/OASIS/Zep application to be installed, this repository
vendors exactly the subset the container images copy onto `PYTHONPATH`. Those
files are:

| Path in this repository | Origin | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| `backend/app/__init__.py` | MiroFish, modified | AGPL-3.0 |
| `backend/app/config.py` | MiroFish, unmodified | AGPL-3.0 |
| `backend/app/utils/llm_client.py` | MiroFish, modified | AGPL-3.0 |
| `backend/app/utils/__init__.py` | empty file created by this export | — |
| `backend/app/protocol/` | kswarm, original work | AGPL-3.0 |

The modifications, relative to the upstream commit pinned above:

- `backend/app/__init__.py` — the Flask, config and logger imports move inside
  `create_app()` so that `app.protocol` and `app.utils.llm_client` can be
  imported by a worker daemon without Flask installed.
- `backend/app/utils/llm_client.py` — deterministic completion parameters, a
  guard for a `None` message body returned by some OpenAI-compatible servers,
  and a version hash over the endpoint and model name.

Two further engine files are modified in the source tree and are **not** vendored
here, because nothing in this repository imports them:
`backend/app/services/__init__.py` and `backend/app/services/simulation_runner.py`.
Both changes make package-level imports lazy for the same reason as
`backend/app/__init__.py`.


## Other components

- The Bonsol callback parsing in `solana/` (published separately as
  `kswarm-protocol`) is hand-rolled and imports nothing from Bonsol.
- The Solana program itself is published under Apache-2.0 at
  https://github.com/agent-k-ai/kswarm-protocol; it imports nothing from the
  engine.
- Third-party Python, Rust and Node dependencies keep their own licences; see
  the lockfiles.
